cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset or code, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "Machine Learning for Healthcare Accessibility: Developing a Pharmacy Desert Index for U.S. Counties — Data and Code"
version: 3.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-16
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/RafatMahmudHridoy/Pharmacy-Desert"
abstract: >-
  Dataset and analysis notebook for a study that classifies the current
  pharmacy-desert status of 734 counties in seven U.S. states with machine
  learning and builds a descriptive Pharmacy Desert Index (PDI) from the SHAP
  importance of the selected XGBoost model. Predictors come from the 2021
  County Health Rankings release; the outcome follows Nguyen et al.'s county
  definition (more than 50% of the population living in pharmacy-desert census
  tracts). Version 3.0.0 supersedes versions 1.0.0 and 2.0.0.
keywords:
  - pharmacy deserts
  - machine learning
  - XGBoost
  - SHAP
  - composite index
  - healthcare access
  - county-level analysis
